"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 (Alpine 3.23, OpenSSH 10.2p1) and baseline sshd config/host keys\",\"Generated an ed25519 SSH CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca\",\"Signed /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub as a host certificate (10-year validity, principals node1/IP/localhost) producing ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub\",\"Added 'HostCertificate /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub' to sshd_config, validated with sshd -t, restarted sshd via OpenRC\",\"Verified a client with only '@cert-authority * <CA pubkey>' in known_hosts (no host key pinned) connects and sshd's certificate is accepted\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline and confirmed sshd enabled at boot via rc-update\",\"Issued a backgrounded reboot so the ack returned before disconnect, polled until node reconnected, confirmed new boot_id with low uptime\",\"Post-reboot, confirmed sshd active, host certificate file/config intact, and re-ran CA-trust-only SSH connection test showing successful certificate-based host verification\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"SSH CA created and host presents a CA-signed certificate\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-99bb780812304a4c\",\"cmd-9774ee0623354d04\",\"cmd-9ca4109497674518\",\"cmd-8387c01f04d6420c\"],\"summary\":\"CA keypair generated at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca; ed25519 host key signed into ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub; sshd_config updated with HostCertificate directive, config validated, sshd restarted.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Client trusting only the CA (not pinning host key) connects without a host-key prompt/mismatch\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-360a00b9de8c4f1c\",\"cmd-8c49a07656074540\"],\"summary\":\"known_hosts contained only an '@cert-authority * <CA pubkey>' line (no host key entries). ssh debug output shows 'Host is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate' and proceeds to auth (Permission denied on publickey is expected/unrelated to host verification).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-49ea43b06a354cd2\",\"cmd-00f7e18c08be4180\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 555f40d8... and uptime 64s; confirmed sshd status started and enabled in OpenRC default runlevel before restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect, and restart is proven via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f648b97775454a32\",\"cmd-83492d50544947b7\",\"cmd-07a85b5f65be4106\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sleep 1; reboot' returned its ack immediately; subsequent polls hit connection reset/timeout during reboot; reconnect showed new boot_id 651f5bb3... (differs from baseline) with uptime 15.88s, proving an actual restart occurred.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 post-restart recovery of required services/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8c49a07656074540\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, sshd status is 'started', the HostCertificate config and signed cert file are intact, and the CA-trust-only SSH connection test again confirms successful certificate-based host verification, proving both the sshd service and the SSH CA setup persisted and recovered.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created an SSH host CA on node1, signed the ed25519 host key into a certificate, configured sshd to present it via HostCertificate, and verified a client trusting only the CA (no host-key pinning) accepts the connection. Restarted node1 per protocol, confirmed a changed boot identity, and re-verified sshd and cert-based host verification recovered post-reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 (Alpine 3.23, OpenSSH 10.2p1) and baseline sshd config/host keys","Generated an ed25519 SSH CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca","Signed /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub as a host certificate (10-year validity, principals node1/IP/localhost) producing ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub","Added 'HostCertificate /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub' to sshd_config, validated with sshd -t, restarted sshd via OpenRC","Verified a client with only '@cert-authority * <CA pubkey>' in known_hosts (no host key pinned) connects and sshd's certificate is accepted","Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline and confirmed sshd enabled at boot via rc-update","Issued a backgrounded reboot so the ack returned before disconnect, polled until node reconnected, confirmed new boot_id with low uptime","Post-reboot, confirmed sshd active, host certificate file/config intact, and re-ran CA-trust-only SSH connection test showing successful certificate-based host verification"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SSH CA created and host presents a CA-signed certificate","command_ids":["cmd-99bb780812304a4c","cmd-9774ee0623354d04","cmd-9ca4109497674518","cmd-8387c01f04d6420c"],"summary":"CA keypair generated at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca; ed25519 host key signed into ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub; sshd_config updated with HostCertificate directive, config validated, sshd restarted."},{"requirement":"Client trusting only the CA (not pinning host key) connects without a host-key prompt/mismatch","command_ids":["cmd-360a00b9de8c4f1c","cmd-8c49a07656074540"],"summary":"known_hosts contained only an '@cert-authority * <CA pubkey>' line (no host key entries). ssh debug output shows 'Host is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate' and proceeds to auth (Permission denied on publickey is expected/unrelated to host verification)."},{"requirement":"Node1 healthy baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-49ea43b06a354cd2","cmd-00f7e18c08be4180"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 555f40d8... and uptime 64s; confirmed sshd status started and enabled in OpenRC default runlevel before restart."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect, and restart is proven via changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-f648b97775454a32","cmd-83492d50544947b7","cmd-07a85b5f65be4106"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'sleep 1; reboot' returned its ack immediately; subsequent polls hit connection reset/timeout during reboot; reconnect showed new boot_id 651f5bb3... (differs from baseline) with uptime 15.88s, proving an actual restart occurred."},{"requirement":"Node1 post-restart recovery of required services/data","command_ids":["cmd-8c49a07656074540"],"summary":"After reboot, sshd status is 'started', the HostCertificate config and signed cert file are intact, and the CA-trust-only SSH connection test again confirms successful certificate-based host verification, proving both the sshd service and the SSH CA setup persisted and recovered."}]},"ttft_ms":1615,"type":"result","duration_ms":101163,"uuid":"a8d3927e-96c0-44ff-ac31-8288d49b069f","ttft_stream_ms":706,"time_to_request_ms":79,"first_content_frame_ms":706,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
